# =============================================================================
# SUBTEXTURE BASE ONTOLOGY
# =============================================================================
#
# The foundational base ontology that sits under everything in the Subtexture
# ecosystem (Pan, Ravel, git-lex, and the kits built above them).
#
# LAYER DISCIPLINE: this file is pure base. It declares ZERO application or kit
# prefixes and never points upward at git-lex:, pan:, or ravel:. Each upper
# ontology imports `subtexture:`, subclasses `subtexture:Thing` (or `Set` /
# `NamedGraph`), keeps its own namespace in stored data, and bridges its
# properties to `subtexture:*` via `owl:equivalentProperty` in its own file.
#
# CHANGELOG
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v0.8.0 (2026-11-27, ruled by goodlux): QUERY SERVICE TARGET.
#   (1) + `subtexture:service` (`owl:DatatypeProperty`, domain `subtexture:Query`,
#       range `xsd:string`, `owl:cardinality 1` — required, exactly one).
#       Values are the service names as in addresses and Syrinx `--engine`:
#       `git-lex`, `pan`, `ravel`, `horae`, `punctum`, or `syrinx`.
#       `syrinx` marks a cross-store federated query whose SPARQL text names
#       each store in `SERVICE` blocks; every other value marks a plain
#       single-store query with no `SERVICE` block.
#   (2) Replaces the v0.4.0 "DELIBERATELY NOT DONE: target-store flags on Query"
#       decision: a single-store query has no `SERVICE` block to say where it
#       goes, and tools installed standalone without Syrinx need to know which
#       service owns a saved Query stored in a git-lex repository.
#   (3) Each app's own `Query` class declares its own `<app>:service` with an
#       `owl:equivalentProperty subtexture:service` bridge (`git-lex:service`,
#       `pan:service`, `punctum:service`, etc.).
#
# v0.7.0 (2026-11-22, ruled by goodlux): UNIVERSAL AUTHOR ON THING.
#   (1) + `subtexture:author` (`owl:DatatypeProperty`, domain `subtexture:Thing`,
#       range `xsd:string`, multi-valued `0..*` — no `maxCardinality` restriction
#       so co-authored Things list every contributor).
#   (2) Expected value convention:
#       - `"{username}-on-{substrate}"` when a runtime model/substrate is known
#         (e.g. `"tr1pl3x-on-gemini-4-carbon-medium"`, `"s3lk13-on-claude-fable-5-2"`).
#       - Bare `"{username}"` when no model substrate applies or is known —
#         including human authors (`"goodlux"`, never `"-on-carbon"` which
#         collides with model names like `gemini-4-carbon-medium`) and inbound
#         peer turns where no model was reported (`"spacegoat"`).
#       - Because canonical usernames are hyphen-free (`^[a-z0-9]+$`), the first
#         `"-on-"` splits `{username}` and `{substrate}` losslessly. Writers must
#         never invent hardcoded fallback model names when a session's model
#         cannot be read; emit bare `"{username}"` instead.
#   DELIBERATELY NOT DONE: separate `subtexture:substrate` or `subtexture:model`
#   property on `Thing` (unordered multi-valued sets lose which co-author ran on
#   which substrate, and `pan:model` names vision enrichment models rather than
#   speaker substrates).
#
# v0.6.0 (2026-11-19, ruled by goodlux): NAMED GRAPH DESCRIPTORS & ACCESS METADATA.
#   (1) Store-scoped NamedGraph IRIs (https://repolex.ai/{squad}/{user}/{app}/NamedGraph/{id}):
#       every named graph descriptor lives in its Oxigraph store's unnamed graph
#       with the graph's own IRI as subject (no sd:name indirection).
#   (2) Structural classes under `subtexture:NamedGraph`:
#       + `subtexture:OntologyGraph` — T-box ontology graphs (left unrewritten
#         by `calamus`).
#       + `subtexture:DefaultGraph` — graphs included in the store's default
#         view when a query carries no `GRAPH` clause.
#   (3) Ownership & access properties on `subtexture:NamedGraph` (`owner` max 1,
#       `visibility` max 1):
#       + `subtexture:owner` (`owl:ObjectProperty`, range `subtexture:Thing`) —
#         the Soul or entity that owns the graph (always allowed).
#       + `subtexture:visibility` (`owl:DatatypeProperty`, range
#         `subtexture:VisibilityValue` = `"private" | "shared" | "public"`) —
#         `"private"` is the safe default when omitted; `"shared"` grants read
#         access to `readableBy`; `"public"` is world-readable.
#       + `subtexture:readableBy` (`owl:ObjectProperty`, multi-valued `0..*`) —
#         Soul or squad IRIs permitted to read the graph when `visibility` is
#         `"shared"`.
#
# v0.5.0 (2026-11-17, ruled by goodlux): PARAMETERIZED QUERIES.
#   (1) + `subtexture:parameter` (`owl:DatatypeProperty`, domain
#       `subtexture:Query`, range `xsd:string`, multi-valued `0..*`) — declares
#       one query parameter per value using `name[:kind][=default]`, where
#       `name` is the SPARQL variable name without `?`, `kind` is one of
#       `string`, `integer`, `decimal`, `boolean`, `date`, `dateTime`, or `iri`
#       (no `kind` means `string` always — never guessed from how a value
#       looks; `iri` accepts `<ns/Class/id>` or bare `ns/Class/id`), and
#       `=default` makes the parameter optional with that default value. Values
#       are bound as typed RDF terms, never substituted as raw text.
#   (2) Removed the v0.4.0 "zero parameters" constraint from `subtexture:Query`
#       and `subtexture:sparql` comments; `subtexture:sparql` holds the query
#       with parameters unbound.
#
# v0.4.0 (2026-11-16, ruled by goodlux): QUERIES AND SMART SETS.
#   (1) + `subtexture:Query` (`rdfs:subClassOf subtexture:Thing`) — a saved
#       read-only SPARQL 1.1 query as a first-class Thing, inheriting `id`,
#       `title`, `description`, `abstract`, `cue`, `relatedToId`, `createdDate`,
#       and `updatedDate` from the base. Cross-store federated queries need no
#       separate class or target property: an ordinary `Query` whose SPARQL text
#       uses standard `SERVICE <https://repolex.ai/ontology/.../>` blocks is run
#       by Syrinx and refused plainly by single-store daemons.
#   (2) + `subtexture:sparql` (`owl:DatatypeProperty`, domain `subtexture:Query`,
#       range `xsd:string`, `owl:maxCardinality 1` on `subtexture:Query`) — the
#       executable SPARQL 1.1 query text verbatim, with zero parameters in v1.
#       `maxCardinality 1` at the base allows document layers (`git-lex:Query`)
#       to derive the triple from the markdown body fence without forcing a
#       duplicate frontmatter key, while graph-only stores (`pan:Query`) tighten
#       to `owl:cardinality 1` on their own class.
#   (3) Smart sets via `relatedToId` (ruled by goodlux):
#       - A `Set` that links a `Query` via `relatedToId` IS a smart set — no
#         separate boolean flag that could drift out of step.
#       - At most ONE `Query` per `Set` (`owl:maxQualifiedCardinality 1` on
#         `subtexture:Set` over `subtexture:relatedToId` to `subtexture:Query`);
#         a need one query cannot meet points to missing infrastructure rather
#         than multiple queries on one set.
#       - No mixing query-computed results and hand-added members in one `Set`;
#         combine a smart set and a hand set via a collection `Set` (a `Set` of
#         two or more `Set`s) instead.
#   DELIBERATELY NOT DONE (in v0.4.0; revisited in v0.5.0 & v0.8.0): query
#   parameters in v1 (added in v0.5.0); target-store flags on `Query` (revisited
#   in v0.8.0 as `subtexture:service` because a single-store query has no
#   `SERVICE` block to say where it goes).
#
# v0.3.0 (2026-11-16, ruled by goodlux): PURE BASE INVERSION & ALL EIGHT UNIVERSALS.
#   (1) Pure base layering: removed `@prefix git-lex:`, removed the upward
#       `git-lex:Thing` / `git-lex:NamedGraph` subclass axioms and `git-lex:*`
#       `owl:equivalentProperty` bridges from this file, and re-ranged
#       `subtexture:id` and `subtexture:relatedToId` from `git-lex:Thing` to
#       `subtexture:Thing`. Each app owns its own namespace and declares its
#       subclassing and `owl:equivalentProperty` bridges in its own ontology.
#   (2) Eight universal Thing properties at the base: + `subtexture:title`,
#       + `subtexture:description`, + `subtexture:abstract`, + `subtexture:cue`
#       join `id`, `relatedToId`, `createdDate`, and `updatedDate` on
#       `subtexture:Thing`. Document-carrier properties (`fileId`, `substrate`,
#       `kitManaged`) remain up on `git-lex:Thing`.
#   (3) Optional `id` at the base (`owl:maxCardinality 1`): `subtexture:Thing`
#       relaxes `subtexture:id` from `owl:cardinality 1` to `owl:maxCardinality 1`
#       alongside `title`, `description`, `abstract`, `createdDate`, and
#       `updatedDate`. Derived Things whose subject IRI IS their identity
#       (`ravel:Turn`, `ravel:Memory`) never emit a self-loop `id` triple;
#       layers that emit an explicit `id` triple (`git-lex:Thing`, `pan:Node`)
#       enforce `owl:cardinality 1` on their own class.
#   (4) - `subtexture:Sequence`: deleted outright (zero instances anywhere;
#       `copia:Sequence` retired in copia 0.41.0, Pan sets are unordered, and
#       Ravel orders transcripts via `parentTurn` + `timestamp` and OptMem via
#       integer `logStart` / `logEnd`). `subtexture:Set` and
#       `subtexture:NamedGraph` remain.
#   DELIBERATELY NOT DONE: adding a set-side `member` property on
#   `subtexture:Set` (membership lives on the member via `relatedToId`);
#   rewriting stored app graphs to emit `subtexture:*` predicates directly
#   (each app owns its namespace and bridges via `owl:equivalentProperty`).
#
# v0.2.0 (2026-09-21, ruled by goodlux): NAMED GRAPH VOCABULARY.
#   (1) + `subtexture:NamedGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf sd:NamedGraph` —
#   the ecosystem-wide root for typed named graph descriptors in any Subtexture
#   store (git-lex, Pan, Ravel, etc.), anchored to W3C SPARQL Service
#   Description `sd:NamedGraph`.
#
# v0.1.0 (2026-09-16, ruled by goodlux): FIRST CUT.
#   (1) + `subtexture:Thing` — the universal root entity with its own identity
#   and lifetime, independent of the file or record that carries it.
#   (2) Foundational properties on `subtexture:Thing`: `id`, `createdDate`,
#   `updatedDate`, and `relatedToId`.
#   (3) + `subtexture:Set` — an unordered collection of Things.
# =============================================================================

@prefix subtexture: <https://repolex.ai/ontology/subtexture/> .
@prefix owl:        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:        <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:       <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:        <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix sd:         <http://www.w3.org/ns/sparql-service-description#> .

<https://repolex.ai/ontology/subtexture> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Subtexture Base Ontology" ;
    rdfs:comment "The foundational base ontology for the Subtexture ecosystem: Thing, Set, Query, NamedGraph, and the universal Thing properties." ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.8.0" .


# =============================================================================
# 1. THE UNIVERSAL ENTITY (subtexture:Thing)
# =============================================================================
# A Thing is an entity with its own identity and lifetime, independent of any
# file or carrier. Authored document classes (via git-lex:Thing) and derived
# graph-only classes (Pan's pan:Node, Ravel's Turn and Memory) are all Things.
#
# Each application owns its own namespace in stored data (`pan:*`, `ravel:*`,
# `git-lex:*`) and bridges its universal properties to `subtexture:*` via
# `owl:equivalentProperty` in its own ontology file.
# =============================================================================

subtexture:Thing a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Thing" ;
    rdfs:comment "Universal root entity with its own identity and lifetime, independent of any file or store." .


# --- The Nine Universal Properties on Thing ----------------------------------

subtexture:id a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "id" ;
    rdfs:comment "Which Thing this node IS, written <namespace/Class/identifier>; never write a bare token." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range subtexture:Thing .

subtexture:title a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "title" ;
    rdfs:comment "One short display name for this Thing. Single-valued — overwrite it, do not repeat the key." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

subtexture:description a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "description" ;
    rdfs:comment "CURATED — a short deliberate summary software may read. Single-valued — do not repeat the key." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

subtexture:abstract a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "abstract" ;
    rdfs:comment "GENERATED — machine summary automation may overwrite; for a curated summary use description." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

subtexture:cue a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "cue" ;
    rdfs:comment "WHEN to reach for this Thing — name a moment with a verb, not a topic; do not repeat the key." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

subtexture:relatedToId a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "relatedToId" ;
    rdfs:comment "Another Thing this one relates to, written <namespace/Class/identifier>; do not repeat the key." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range subtexture:Thing .

subtexture:createdDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "createdDate" ;
    rdfs:comment "When this Thing was first created, ISO-8601 dateTime with offset; do not write a bare date." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

subtexture:updatedDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "updatedDate" ;
    rdfs:comment "When this Thing last changed, ISO-8601 dateTime with offset; maintained by the writer, do not hand-edit." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

# Expected values for `subtexture:author`:
#   - `"{username}-on-{substrate}"` when the runtime model/substrate is known
#     (e.g. `"tr1pl3x-on-gemini-4-carbon-medium"`, `"s3lk13-on-claude-fable-5-2"`).
#   - Bare `"{username}"` when no model substrate applies or is known — always
#     bare for humans (`"goodlux"`, never `"-on-carbon"`) and when a harness or
#     peer header reports no model (`"spacegoat"`). Never guess or hardcode a
#     fallback model id.
#   - Canonical usernames are hyphen-free (`^[a-z0-9]+$`), so the first `"-on-"`
#     splits `{username}` and `{substrate}` without ambiguity. To query an agent
#     across all substrates: `FILTER(?a = "s3lk13" || STRSTARTS(?a, "s3lk13-on-"))`.
#   - Self-reported / session-populated `xsd:string` convention, not cryptographic
#     proof; multi-valued (`0..*`) so co-authors may all be recorded.
subtexture:author a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "author" ;
    rdfs:comment "Who authored this: '{username}-on-{substrate}' when model is known, or bare '{username}' (humans or unknown model); multi-valued — do not repeat the key." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .


# =============================================================================
# 2. COLLECTIONS
# =============================================================================
# Hand-curated membership is written on the member via `relatedToId`, never as
# a set-side `member` list, so membership travels with the member record.
#
# Smart sets (ruled by goodlux): a Set that links a Query via `relatedToId` IS
# a smart set, with at most ONE Query per Set (`owl:maxQualifiedCardinality 1`
# below). Never mix query results and hand-added members in one Set; combine a
# smart set and a hand set via a collection Set (a Set of Sets) instead.
# =============================================================================

subtexture:Set a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:label "Set" ;
    rdfs:comment "An unordered collection of Things; link hand members from the member via relatedToId, or link at most one Query on the Set for a smart set." .


# =============================================================================
# 3. QUERIES
# =============================================================================
# A saved SPARQL 1.1 read query as a first-class Thing. Every Query names the
# one service that runs it via `subtexture:service` (`git-lex`, `pan`, `ravel`,
# `horae`, `punctum`, or `syrinx`). `syrinx` marks a cross-store federated query
# whose `subtexture:sparql` uses standard `SERVICE` blocks; every other value
# marks a plain single-store query against that service. Parameters are declared
# via `subtexture:parameter` as `name[:kind][=default]` and bound as typed RDF
# terms (never pasted as text).
# =============================================================================

subtexture:Query a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf subtexture:Thing ;
    rdfs:label "Query" ;
    rdfs:comment "A saved read-only SPARQL 1.1 query naming its target service (single-store or syrinx federated via SERVICE blocks), optionally parameterized via parameter." .

subtexture:service a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "service" ;
    rdfs:comment "Target service that runs this Query: one of git-lex, pan, ravel, horae, punctum, or syrinx (for cross-store SERVICE queries); required, single-valued." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Query ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

subtexture:sparql a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "sparql" ;
    rdfs:comment "Executable SPARQL 1.1 query string with parameters unbound; single-valued — overwrite it, do not repeat the key." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Query ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

subtexture:parameter a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "parameter" ;
    rdfs:comment "One query parameter as name[:kind][=default] (kinds: string, integer, decimal, boolean, date, dateTime, iri); multi-valued." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:Query ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .


# =============================================================================
# 4. GRAPHS & ACCESS METADATA
# =============================================================================
# Every Oxigraph store's unnamed graph holds one descriptor per named graph in
# that store, using the store-scoped graph IRI itself as subject
# (`https://repolex.ai/{squad}/{user}/{app}/NamedGraph/{id}`, no sd:name).
# Structural role is expressed by subclassing (`OntologyGraph`, `DefaultGraph`);
# ownership and read access are expressed via `owner`, `visibility` ('private'
# default when omitted, 'shared', 'public'), and `readableBy`. Each engine
# emits its own namespace terms and bridges upward here.
# =============================================================================

subtexture:NamedGraph a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf sd:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:label "NamedGraph" ;
    rdfs:comment "A named graph descriptor in a Subtexture Oxigraph store's unnamed graph; its subject IRI IS the named graph IRI." .

subtexture:OntologyGraph a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf subtexture:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:label "Ontology graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "A named graph holding T-box ontology statements rather than A-box store data; query rewriters read it as written." .

subtexture:DefaultGraph a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf subtexture:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:label "Default graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "A named graph included in the store's default view for queries with no GRAPH clause." .

subtexture:VisibilityValue a rdfs:Datatype ;
    owl:oneOf ("private" "shared" "public") .

subtexture:owner a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "owner" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Soul or entity that owns this named graph; always permitted access." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:range subtexture:Thing .

subtexture:visibility a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "visibility" ;
    rdfs:comment "Access policy for this named graph: 'private' (owner only, default when omitted), 'shared' (owner plus readableBy), or 'public'." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:range subtexture:VisibilityValue .

subtexture:readableBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "readableBy" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Soul or squad Thing permitted to read this named graph when visibility is 'shared'; multi-valued." ;
    rdfs:domain subtexture:NamedGraph ;
    rdfs:range subtexture:Thing .


# =============================================================================
# 5. CARDINALITY
# =============================================================================
# Single-valued universals carry `owl:maxCardinality 1` at the base (`cue`,
# `author`, and `relatedToId` are multi-valued, 0..*). `id` is `maxCardinality 1` here rather
# than `cardinality 1` so derived Things whose subject IRI IS their identity
# (`ravel:Turn`, `ravel:Memory`) need no redundant self-loop triple; layers
# that write an explicit `id` triple (`git-lex:Thing`, `pan:Node`) tighten it
# to `owl:cardinality 1` on their own class. Likewise `sparql` is
# `maxCardinality 1` at the base so document carriers (`git-lex:Query`) can
# derive it from the markdown body fence without requiring a frontmatter key.
# =============================================================================

subtexture:Thing rdfs:subClassOf
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:id          ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:title       ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:description ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:abstract    ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:createdDate ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:updatedDate ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] .

subtexture:Set rdfs:subClassOf
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:relatedToId ; owl:onClass subtexture:Query ; owl:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ] .

subtexture:Query rdfs:subClassOf
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:service ; owl:cardinality 1 ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:sparql  ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] .

subtexture:NamedGraph rdfs:subClassOf
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:owner      ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] ,
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty subtexture:visibility ; owl:maxCardinality 1 ] .
